            <ArticleTitle>Pain with amniocentesis and transabdominal CVS.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>308-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fifty consecutive patients undergoing transabdominal chorionic villus sampling (CVS) and 52 undergoing amniocentesis completed a questionnaire following the procedure to determine the amount of pain they experienced. Mild pain, discomfort only or no pain was reported by 96% undergoing amniocentesis and 90% with CVS. Moderate or severe pain was reported after completion of the CVS by 8% and following amniocentesis by 2%. Both procedures were well tolerated.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
